WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.638
A periodic signal repeats the same cycle over and over. The simplest is the pure tone, a sine: in the spectrum it is a single line.

2
00:00:10.128 --> 00:00:18.969
A complex periodic signal adds several sines whose frequencies are multiples of a fundamental. It still repeats, and its spectrum has several lines.

3
00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:29.546
An impulse is an extremely short click: all its energy is in one instant. Its spectrum is flat, because it contains every frequency equally.

4
00:00:32.089 --> 00:00:39.189
White noise is aperiodic: it never repeats a cycle. It spreads its energy over all frequencies, at random.

5
00:00:41.752 --> 00:00:46.688
On the same time scale you can see the difference: three signals that repeat and one that does not.
